{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>It is not good that the man should be alone.</b> For in every place where there is divergence and strife, the good is not found there — for this reason 'כִּי טוֹב' was not said on the second day, because in it strife was created, for every number involving two contains division and separation. And if so, if the man and the woman had each been formed from its own material separately, then there would be two divided bodies and the good would not cleave to them, because they would be lacking love and unity, and they would be close to coming to separation and quarrel and to creating a breach between those joined together. And man is political by nature, needing love and unity more than all other living creatures. Therefore He said that it would not be good if the man were formed from one material and the woman from a different material. Therefore 'I will make for him a help' — when they would be from one material, then each would be a help and a benefit to the other, and they would stand facing each other, this one opposite that one, for this indicates love, as it is stated (Psalms 16:8): 'שִׁוִּיתִי ה׳ לְנֶגְדִּי תָמִיד' — whose meaning is not an opposition of strife, but an opposition of love like the face to the water, to exclude the case when strife is present, where each one turns his back and not his face to his fellow. Therefore it says 'אֶעֱשֶׂה לּוֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ'." "And some say 'לֹא טוֹב' — that the man is not called a doer of good in the commandments of HaShem, blessed be He, when he is alone and has no adversary to incline him toward evil. Therefore 'אֶעֱשֶׂה לוֹ עֵזֶר כְּנֶגְדּוֹ' — for in that his wife stands opposite him to entice him toward evil and he does not listen to her and prevails over her, then he is called a doer of good. For there is no righteous man on earth who does good when he does so out of compulsion and cannot sin, but only when he has the possibility to sin yet escapes it."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:26:47.399771303Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}